      "cause": "Package is 168px, Notes is 330px, and the resulting table extends 113px beyond the viewport."
    },
    {
      "design": "d3r4C",
      "good": "Notes read comfortably in the full view, and the internal package name has more room. The compact audit fields retain their clear alignment.",
      "problems": "The package name still occupies three lines, so its extra width brings little height benefit. Less of each note is visible initially, and the advisory URL still wraps.",
      "cause": "Increasing Package to 220px and Notes to 350px makes the table 185px wider than the viewport without reducing its overall height compared with d3r4B."
    },
    {
      "design": "d3r2A",
      "good": "All fields remain visible together. The advisory URL wraps at a slash rather than inside the word seen in d3r4A, while the audit fields stay legible and aligned.",
